--- a/docs/MARTY_SEMILEPTONIC_CHIRAL_TREELEVEL.md
+++ b/docs/MARTY_SEMILEPTONIC_CHIRAL_TREELEVEL.md
@@ -36,3 +36,20 @@ covers and supplies its own F/O term by term.  All OneLoop controls are
 unchanged.  HyperIso does not scan permutations during production calculations;
 projection discovery is an explicit Python diagnostic step and the accepted
 profile should be frozen for scans and fits.
+
+## Electroweak input scheme for semileptonic one-loop matching
+
+For one-loop `C9`, `C10`, `CP9`, and `CP10` matching, HyperIso rewrites the
+residual MARTY electromagnetic coupling in the extracted Wilson expression as
+
+```text
+e_loop = sqrt(sqrt(2) * G_F) * M_Z * sin(2 * theta_W).
+```
+
+This enforces the tree-level EW identities assumed by the reduced SuperIso
+semileptonic formulae. The rewrite is deliberately **not** applied to a
+non-zero TreeLevel BSM coefficient: direct Z' / leptoquark matching continues
+to use the physical `alpha_em` normalization of the WET operator basis.
+
+The distinction removes the EW-scheme normalization offset seen in SM/THDM
+loop matching without changing direct tree-level neutral-current benchmarks.
